    language en
    text "Compound interest calculation\n\nFormula: A = P(1 + r/n)^(n*t)\nP = {principal} USD\nr = {rate} ({percent}% annual)\nn = {periods_per_year} ({frequency})\nt = {years} years\n\nStep 1: periodic rate = r/n = {rate}/{periods_per_year} = {periodic_rate}\nStep 2: number of periods = n*t = {periods_per_year}*{years} = {periods}\nStep 3: A = {principal} * (1 + {periodic_rate})^{periods}\nFinal amount: {final_amount} USD"
